    <IRS990ScheduleO documentId="IRS990ScheduleO" softwareId="24020490" softwareVersionNum="2024v5.2">
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section A, Line 6</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>MEMBERS</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 11b</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>COPY OF FORM 990 IS REVIEWED BY THE EXECUTIVE COMMITTEE BEFORE IT IS FILED.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 12c</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>If any disclosures of conflict of interested are made, the President and/or Board of Direcotrs: (A)Take no action, if no action is warrented, (b) Assure full disclosure to the Board of Directors and other individuals covered by this policy,(C ) Ask that the person recuse themselves from participating in related discussio or voting (D) Ask the person to resign from their position in the organization, or if the person refuses to resign, become subject for possible removal in accordance with the organizations bylaws and removal procedures. Executive Director and Staff monitor ongoing and proposed transactions for conflicts of interest and disclose them to the President and Board of Directors in order to deal with potential conflicts.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 15a</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>The review process begins with the convening of the Executive Officer Review Task Force. The Task Force is comprised of the Officers of the organization. The Chair of the group is the sitting President of the SCRHA. The Task Force is charged with reviewing the organizational and individual performance of the key employee and making a salary recommendation to the Board of Directors. Additionally, the task force uses salary surveys to ensure that the individual is fairly compensated for his/her position.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section C, Line 19</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>GOVERNING DOCUMENTS, POLICIES, AND FINANCIAL STATEMENTS ARE AVAILABLE UPON REQUEST.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART V, LINE 2A &amp; PART IX, LINE 7 &amp; SCHEDULE J</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE ORGANIZATION LEASES EMPLOYEES FROM A RELATED ORGANIZATION, SAN DIEGO MULTI-HOUSING CORP (SDMHC). SDMHC IS RESPONSIBLE FOR ALL PAYROLL ACTIVITY FOR BOTH ENTITIES. THE PAYROLL REPORTS ARE FILED UNDER SDMHC, NO W-2S HAVE BEEN FILED DIRECTLY BY SOUTHERN CALIFORNIA RENTAL HOUSING ASSOCIATION.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
    </IRS990ScheduleO>
